@startuml ethernet_cbs_Sequence_Diagram

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

title Ethernet CBS (IEEE 802.1Qav Credit-Based Shaper) Example Project

actor "Application\n(hal_entry)" as APP
participant "CBS Example EP\n(cbs_example_run)" as EP
participant "Layer3 Switch\n(r_layer3_switch)" as L3SW
participant "GWCA TX\n(cbs_send_frames_burst)" as GWCA
participant "Host PC\n(RTT Viewer + Wireshark)" as PC
participant "Traffic Source\n(PC / Linux host script)" as GEN

legend top left
**loop**  : Repeated every cycle/interval
**alt**   : Branch on condition
**opt**   : Optional / conditional
**note**  : Key design explanation
endlegend

== System Initialization (once per boot) ==

APP -> EP: cbs_example_run()
EP -> L3SW: cbs_open()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_Open(g_layer3_switch0)
L3SW --> EP: FSP_SUCCESS
EP -> L3SW: R_RMAC0/1->MRAFC = 0x03C703C7UL
note over EP, L3SW #FFF9C4
RMAC's receive filter defaults to non-promiscuous and
is not touched by Open(). Without this write, externally
received frames addressed to the synthetic test MACs
(44:44:44:00:00:0A/0B) are dropped before they ever
reach MAC-table classification (port-to-port modes only;
CPU-injected traffic bypasses this filter).
end note

EP -> EP: wait for ETH0 + ETH1 link UP (5 s timeout)
EP -> PC: console: "[CBS] ETH0 link: UP   ETH1 link: UP"

== First Mode Selection (the only blocking prompt) ==

EP -> PC: print menu ([1]..[6])
PC -> EP: type a mode number, 1-6
note right of PC #D4E6F1
[1]-[3] port-to-port : disabled / Q0 only / Q1 only
[4]-[6] CPU-generated: disabled / Q0 only / Q1 only
end note

== Mode Loop (repeats on every mode change -- no stop step) ==

loop forever
    EP -> L3SW: cbs_clear_mac_table()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_ConfigureTable() (reset)
    EP -> EP: build the row table for the selected mode
    note over EP #FFF9C4
    Isolated modes ([2]/[3]/[5]/[6]) copy the use-case
    table and zero the OTHER queue's MAC, so only one
    queue is classified and shaped at a time.
    end note
    EP -> L3SW: cbs_configure_mac_table()\n-> ConfigureTable() + AddTableEntry() x1-2
    note over EP, L3SW #D4E6F1
    dest MAC -> IPV queue (internal_priority_update_value),
    steered from the mode's source port:
    Port1 (external) or Port2 (CPU inject).
    end note
    L3SW --> EP: FSP_SUCCESS
    EP -> L3SW: cbs_configure_bandwidth()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_ConfigurePort(Port0, cbs_cfg)
    note over EP, L3SW #D4E6F1
    CBS enabled : Q0 = 10 %, Q1 = 30 % of the link speed
    CBS disabled: all-zero config (shaping off)
    Queues being switched off are committed explicitly
    (the driver commits only the queues it enables).
    Port0 is the CBS-shaped egress port in every mode.
    end note
    L3SW --> EP: FSP_SUCCESS
    EP -> PC: console: "CBS: ENABLED/disabled", "Qn: N% bandwidth",\n"MAC table entries: N", "CBS active in hardware (queue mask)"

    alt CPU-generated modes [4]-[6]
        EP -> L3SW: cbs_tx_queue_create()\n-> R_LAYER3_SWITCH_CreateDescriptorQueue()
        EP -> EP: cbs_tx_burst_prepare(dst MAC, queue)
        note over EP, L3SW #FFF9C4
        One fixed frame/descriptor is built once. The queue
        index is written into the descriptor's own ipv field --
        it is NOT inferred from the destination MAC.
        end note
        loop every cycle, until a different mode number is typed
            EP -> GWCA: cbs_send_frames_burst()
            GWCA -> L3SW: SetDescriptor() until the ring is full\n(CBS_TX_DESC_NUM = 4)
            GWCA -> L3SW: one StartDescriptorQueue() for the whole batch
            note right of GWCA #FFF9C4
            Batched submission lets GWCA auto-chain through
            the queued descriptors. 4 slots gives a smooth,
            near-continuous stream to the credit shaper.
            end note
        end loop
    else Port-to-port modes [1]-[3]
        GEN -> L3SW: near-MTU frames into ETH1 (Port1)\n(--mode flood --queue 0 | 1)
        note right of GEN #D4E6F1
        Needs several hundred Mbps of offered load to
        prove a cap -- use a source that delivers >400-500 Mbps.
        end note
        loop every 1 ms, until a different mode number is typed
            EP -> EP: idle-wait
        end loop
    end alt

    L3SW --> PC: shaped egress on ETH0 (Port0)\n-> Wireshark I/O Graph: Q0 ~100 Mbps, Q1 ~300 Mbps

    opt roughly once a second
        EP -> EP: re-poll ETH0/ETH1 link status
        opt a link is down
            EP -> PC: console: "[CBS] WARNING: ETH0 link: .. ETH1 link: .. -- frames cannot flow on a down link"
        end opt
    end opt

    opt a different valid mode number typed (non-blocking check)
        PC -> EP: new mode number
        EP -> EP: adopt it, go back to the top of the loop
    else the same number typed again
        EP -> PC: console: "[CBS] Mode N is already active."
    end opt
end loop

@enduml
